hw/sh4: ze0 SD host (SDHI/TMIO-style) ports, SDHI interrupts, SCIF stubs (TODO M8.C10).

hw/sh4/ze0_sdhi.c (new): a minimal Renesas SDHI/TMIO-style SD host with
16-bit registers and no address shift, on QEMU's SD bus.  Evidence (EU2011
SDHC.dll): the card-detect read fn 0x039bcedc reports a card only when bit
5 of SD_INFO1 (+0x1c) is set; the host init fn 0x039bcf20 writes the
SD_INFO1/2 masks (+0x20/+0x22), SDIO_INFO1_MASK (+0x38) and CC_EXT_MODE
(+0xd8).  Commands complete synchronously (SD_INFO1.RSPEND); data moves
by PIO through SD_BUF0 (SD_INFO2.BRE/BWE, SD_INFO1.ACCESSEND).  DMA mode
(CC_EXT_MODE bit 1) is logged and not modelled: the HPB DMAC is row M8.C1.
Option trace logs every register access under -d unimp.

hw/sh4/ze0.c: ports 0/1 at 0xffe4c000/0xffe4d000 plus their area-7
aliases 0x1fe4c000/0x1fe4d000; -drive if=sd,index=N gives port N a
sd-card (the size must be a power of two: use a qcow2 overlay over a card
image).  sdhi=off keeps the P4 catch-all (negative control);
sdhi-trace=on turns on the register trace.  SCIF channels 0-5 and 7 get
sh_serial models (and area-7 aliases, also for the debug channel 6):
serial_scif.dll fn 0x0398e888 spins in kernel mode on SCFSR.TEND of
channel 1 through 0x1fe41010, which reads 0 in the catch-all and starved
device.exe once the SD path ran; scif-stubs=off keeps the old map.  The
proper SCIF model is row M8.C2.

hw/sh4/ze0_intc.c: sources SDHI0/SDHI1 at INTEVT 0xae0/0xb00 (OAL
interrupt table 0x88005c48: ISR fn 0x8803fcdc/0x8803fd40, IntrPrio 9,
SYSINTR 0x1f/0x20), INT2 bit 29 (SDHC.dll's InterruptInitialize is
followed by INT2MSKCR = 0x20080000; both ISRs test bit 29 of INT2 +0x3c,
which now reads back the asserted SD sources), priority field INT2PRI7
bits 20:16 (derived from the TMU layout, not documented).

Evidence and controls: docs/experiments/EXP-2026-11-20-M8.C10-sd-host.md
(C-1460..C-1464).  Base: QEMU 8.2.10 + the earlier patches (sorts after
ze0-0007).

This file is the QEMU 11.1.3 form of the patch (TODO M8.A11): the text
above was written for the 8.2 series, where the patch was first made;
API names in it that 11.x renamed are listed in PORT-11.1.md.  Base: tag
v11.1.3 plus the earlier patches of this directory, in sorted order.

